"""run_campaign.py - the experiment runner for {{CAMPAIGN_TITLE}}.

Runs ONE experiment from a config and writes the full reproducible record. This file is MUTABLE - add
forwards / decoders / preprocessors / search strategies here; it is the plumbing, not the FROZEN
scoring math (that lives in scripts/metric.py).

Usage:
    python scripts/run_campaign.py --baseline                       # experiment 000 (the floor gate)
    python scripts/run_campaign.py --config configs/exp007_foo.json # one experiment
    python scripts/run_campaign.py --preflight --backend <harness> [--smoke] # launch checks (no spend)
    python scripts/run_campaign.py --supervise --backend <harness>          # loop driver

Every run MUST leave behind, for reproducibility:
    configs/exp<NN>_<slug>.json  ·  a results/scoreboard.tsv row  ·  results/result_<NN>.json
    ·  at least one figure in results/images/  ·  a tee'd log in results/diagnostics/
    ·  a reproducibility snapshot in results/snapshots/exp<NN>_<slug>/ (the config + a copy of scripts/)
    ·  an entry appended to results/logbook.md (this script appends the FACTS automatically; the agent
       completes Analysis and NEXT afterward; the runner derives every other line)
The campaign's OWN code - the experiment hooks and the optional seams - is scripts/experiment.py; this
file is the kit's machinery and is never edited per campaign.
    ·  results/checks_<NN>.json - the MECHANICAL checks for this experiment (inside the plausible range,
       change vs the incumbent, comparability, correctness-suite state, save-set), each pass / fail /
       unavailable
A result is not "saved" until it has a scoreboard row, a result_<NN>.json, its figure, AND its snapshot.

ARTIFACT GATES (enforced here, in code - hard gates are gates, not reminders):
  * DELIVERABLE GATE (spend, zero-evaluation units only): a unit that records no score refuses to start
    unless its config names, in `_deliverable`, what will exist on disk afterwards that does not now.
  * SAVE-SET GATE (record): the scoreboard row is appended ONLY after result_<NN>.json, the figure, and
    the snapshot all exist on disk (hard gate 4 as code).
  * MECHANICAL CHECKS (record): after the run, results/checks_<NN>.json records every check the runner
    can make without an agent. It does not block - it makes what the runner already knew READABLE. The
    first is the PLAUSIBLE RANGE (metric.PLAUSIBILITY_BOUNDS, fixed once at setup): a score outside it is
    flagged as a probable implementation error. A check this campaign cannot supply the inputs for is
    recorded `unavailable` with what it NEEDS, never as a silent pass.
Gate violations refuse loudly. The PROMOTE-path gates fail closed; the record-path helpers fail open
(a liveness or logging bug must never lose an experiment). Promotion (current-best,
scoreboard verdict tokens, the project ledger) is gated separately by scripts/guard_promotion.py on
verdict artifacts in results/verdicts/.

Before the experiment runs, two FROZEN-infrastructure gates fire automatically: the metric self-test
(hard-fails if the scorer is unimplemented or fails its scrambled-input null control) and the correctness
suite (its status is recorded to results/correctness_state.json; a RED suite blocks promotion via the
promotion gate).
"""
